---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---

<Base title={`Privacy · ${site.name}`} description={`How ${site.name} handles your books and data.`} path="/privacy">
  <div class="container section">
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: October 2026</p>
      <p class="notice">
        This is a plain-language template and has not been reviewed by a lawyer. Please review it before relying on
        it.
      </p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Your books stay on your devices. If you sign in, we store what is needed to sync your library and reading
        positions between your devices. We do not show ads and we do not use third-party trackers.
      </p>

      <h2>Without an account</h2>
      <p>
        You can use {site.name} without signing in. Your books, reading positions and settings are stored only on
        your device. Text recognition for scanned pages runs on your device. Nothing is sent to us.
      </p>

      <h2>When you sign in</h2>
      <p>You can sign in with email or Google. When you do, we store:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your email address, so you can sign in and we can contact you about your account;</li>
        <li>your library files, so a book you add on one device can appear on your other devices;</li>
        <li>your reading positions, so you can pick up where you left off on any device.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        When you remove a book from your library, it is removed from your other devices and from our storage.
      </p>

      <h2>What we don’t do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We don’t show ads.</li>
        <li>We don’t use third-party trackers or sell your data.</li>
        <li>We don’t read your books or use them for anything other than syncing them for you.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can stop syncing at any time by signing out. To get a copy of your account data or to delete your
        account, email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy? Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
